[?2004l[?2004h>     "answer": "Medications contraindicated or to be avoided with PAXLOVID include: alfuzosin, ranolazine, amiodarone, dronedarone, flecainide, propafenone, quinidine, colchicine (in renal or hepatic impairment), lurasidone, pimozide, silodosin, eplerenone, ivabradine, dihydroergotamine, ergotamine, methylergonovine, lovastatin, simvastatin, voclosporin, lomitapide, eletriptan, ubrogepant, finerenone, naloxegol, sildenafil (Revatio for PAH), triazolam, oral midazolam, flibanserin, and tolvaptan. Strong CYP3A inducers like apalutamide, enzalutamide, carbamazepine, phenobarbital, primidone, phenytoin, rifampin, rifapentine, lumacaftor/ivacaftor, and St. John\u0027s Wort are also contraindicated. Other medications for which concomitant use should be avoided include tamsulosin, encorafenib, ivosidenib, neratinib, venetoclax, ibrutinib, rivaroxaban, voriconazole, aliskiren, ticagrelor, vorapaxar, glecaprevir/pibrentasvir, everolimus, sirolimus, salmeterol, rimegepant, suvorexant, and tadalafil (for PAH).",
[?2004l[?2004h>     "citations": [
